Everything is working now.

**What was wrong:** The `pip` Python package files had been deleted from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/`, but the metadata directory (`pip-24.3.1.dist-info`) was left behind. This caused `import pip` to fail with `ModuleNotFoundError` because pip's entry point script tried to import the module but the actual `pip/` directory was gone.

**What fixed it:** I removed the stale `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` metadata directory and re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade`, which extracted the bundled `pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl` from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip/_bundled/` and restored the package.

